      {
        "id": 91311,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-16T06:25:27.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Quantum Mechanics might be interpreted as suggesting that true randomness is indeed possible.&nbsp; Then again, quantum mechanics can be interpreted as saying all sorts of nonsense if you look at pop-science reports of it from a layman's perspective.&nbsp; I have no idea what it actually says, and enjoy playing with the obviously-not-actually-right implications in fiction, but seeing it used that way but the otherwise-amazing David Brin has definitely made me wince a bit, so I should be careful how I employ these tropes in my own work.</p>",
